  "final_text": "I haven't calculated anything yet. One thing has to be settled first: **is the `amount` column in `monthly_revenue.csv` the MRR at month-end, or the change in MRR during the month?**\n\nThere's no metric definitions file, so nothing says what `amount` means. The April 2026 rows are all negative (Enterprise −13,285, Mid-Market −3,080, SMB −3,595), and MRR at month-end can't be negative. So it looks like `amount` is the monthly change (net new MRR), not the month-end balance. If so:\n\n- Ending MRR = starting MRR + the changes. Neither file has a starting MRR. `customer_master.csv` only has customers, segments, plans and status codes, with no revenue figures.\n- I'd need the MRR at a known date, such as end of March 2026 or end of December 2025, and where that figure comes from.\n\nIf you confirm it's the change and give me a starting MRR, I'll calculate month-end MRR for **April, May and June 2026**. Taking today as 1 July 2026, as you said, that's the last complete quarter. I'll give each month separately, by segment and in total, using `monthly_revenue.csv` → `amount`.\n\nThe `status` codes in the customer file (A, C, N) aren't explained either. My guess is active, churned, new, but I'll only use them, for example for customer counts alongside MRR, if you confirm what they mean.",
